  "solution": {
    "text": "The given series is in GP. Hence, its sum $S=\\frac{1\\left\\{(1+x)^{20+1}-1\\right\\}}{(1+x)-1}=\\frac{(1+x)^{21}-1}{x}$\r\nTherefore, the required coefficient of $x^{10}$ in\r\nthe expansion of $(1+x)^{21}-1$\r\n$=$ Coefficient of $x^{11}$ in the expansion of\r\n$$\r\n={ }^{21} C_{11}\r\n$$",
